# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stash — environment configuration
#
# EVERYTHING IN THIS FILE IS OPTIONAL.
#
# Stash builds, installs and runs as a complete footage catalog with none of
# these set. They only enable the optional Google Drive automation, and even
# then you can enter the same values in Settings → Integrations instead of using
# environment variables at all.
#
# Do not commit real credentials. Copy this file to `.env` if you want to use it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Google Drive (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables: folder browsing, recursive scanning, automatic thumbnails, metadata
# sync, rename/move detection, and preview of private files.
#
# Without these, Stash still does: Drive links, local files, web links, search,
# tags, collections, projects, used/unused tracking, usage history, ratings,
# favorites, notes, custom thumbnails, and Open in Google Drive.
#
# Create these at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#   1. Enable the "Google Drive API" for your project
#   2. Create an OAuth client ID of type "Desktop app"
#   3. Paste the values below, or into Settings → Integrations → OAuth client
#
# The client ID is not a secret. The client secret is stored in your OS keychain
# when entered through Settings; if you set it here instead, treat this file as
# sensitive and keep it out of version control.

STASH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
STASH_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=


# ── Notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# * Environment variables take precedence over values saved in Settings.
# * OAuth tokens are NEVER read from or written to this file. They live in the
#   operating system keychain (macOS Keychain / Windows Credential Manager /
#   Linux Secret Service) and never in your .footagedb library.
# * There are no other environment variables. No API endpoints, no telemetry
#   keys, no feature flags — Stash makes no network requests except to Google,
#   and only when you explicitly connect an account.
